clearcote: persona DPR and pointer-origin coherence (clearcote-browser#11 follow-up)

Found by probing the secondary observation in #11 -- persona screen dimensions alongside real
pointer coordinates. All four defects are one shape: a value overridden in ONE accessor while a
second accessor kept reading the real host, so the two disagreed inside a single page load with
nothing for the site to compare against.

1. media_values.cc -- CalculateDevicePixelRatio() honoured only the seeded-persona case and
   ignored --fingerprint-device-pixel-ratio. A persona claiming 2x matched (resolution: 1dppx)
   and fetched the 1x srcset candidate while window.devicePixelRatio said 2.

2. style_resolver_state.cc -- style resolution received document.DevicePixelRatio(), the frame's
   REAL ratio, so CSS image-set() still picked its 1x candidate after srcset and the resolution
   media query were corrected. Patched at the style-resolution call site rather than in
   Document::DevicePixelRatio(), which also feeds layout paths (text_fit_utils, inline_node,
   layout_image_resource) where an override would change rendering, not resource selection.

3./4. local_dom_window.{h,cc} + mouse_event.cc -- window.screenX/screenY were synthesised to fit
   the persona screen while MouseEvent.screenX/screenY carried true desktop coordinates. Since
   screenX - clientX is constant per window position, a page could subtract the two and recover
   the real desktop origin, then compare it against the claimed screen. Measured before the fix:
   the delta moved 88 -> 76 -> 98 as the persona screen changed, while a real machine holds it
   constant. Both now share one origin delta, exposed as
   LocalDOMWindow::PersonaScreenOriginDelta().

Everything is guarded so behaviour is unchanged when no override is active: the control runs still
report 1dppx and fetch the 1x candidates.

Verified on Windows and Linux, persona DPR 2 with and without a persona screen:
  (resolution: 2dppx) matches, srcset takes img2x.png, image-set() takes css2x.png,
  pointer delta constant at 88 across personas.
Audit after the change: 100/100, 179/179 scored checks agree, automation surface 58/58 -- the
MouseEvent change costs nothing on the input path.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_values.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_values.cc
@@ -201,8 +201,16 @@
 }
 
 float MediaValues::CalculateDevicePixelRatio(LocalFrame* frame) {
-  if (base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch(switches::kFingerprint))
-    return static_cast<float>(ungoogled::CurrentPersona().device_pixel_ratio);
+  // clearcote(#11-follow-up): this drives (resolution: Ndppx), srcset selection
+  // and image-set(). It used to honour ONLY the seeded persona, so the direct
+  // --fingerprint-device-pixel-ratio flag moved window.devicePixelRatio while
+  // every media-query-driven channel stayed on the host ratio -- a persona
+  // claiming 2x fetched the 1x images and matched (resolution: 1dppx).
+  // Same resolver as window.devicePixelRatio and Sec-CH-DPR: flag > persona.
+  const double persona_dpr = ungoogled::PersonaDevicePixelRatio();
+  if (persona_dpr > 0) {
+    return static_cast<float>(persona_dpr);
+  }
   return frame->DevicePixelRatio();
 }
 
